The code was written for SigmaM2M, a oneM2M platform, from the public
TALQ OpenAPI definitions (PROVENANCE.md). It contains no code from other
projects. sim/sim.go and sim/ext.go come from SigmaM2M and carry no
per-file copyright header, the convention of the code they come from;
the copyright line above covers them. Files added for this module carry
"Copyright 2026 Abhinav Gautam" and "SPDX-License-Identifier:
Apache-2.0".

Trademarks
----------

TALQ is a trademark of the TALQ Consortium. This module is not made,
endorsed, certified or supported by the TALQ Consortium and is not
affiliated with it; the name is used only to say which protocol it
simulates.

Specifications
--------------

TALQ OpenAPI definitions 2.7.1 and specification 2.7.1,
github.com/TALQ-consortium/TALQ_specification (BSD-3-Clause for the
OpenAPI files): facts only, through the talq module. No file or text of
them is included.

Interop tests (interop/, a separate test-only module)
-----------------------------------------------------

interop reads the three TALQ 2.7.1 OpenAPI files at test time, from a
checkout or downloaded at a pinned commit with their SHA-256 checked;
nothing of them is copied into this repository. It uses
github.com/santhosh-tekuri/jsonschema/v6 (Apache-2.0, Copyright Santhosh
Kumar Tekuri) and its dependency golang.org/x/text (BSD-3-Clause,
Copyright The Go Authors).

Dependencies
------------

- github.com/cB-Sigma/talq (Copyright 2026 Abhinav Gautam, Apache-2.0,
  standard library only).
- The Go standard library (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright The Go Authors).

Test data
---------

Every address, token, device name and asset type in this module is a
made-up demo value; test certificates are generated at run time.
